### Fleet Telemetry Monitoring Service - IntelliJ HTTP Client
### Start the stack first:
###   docker compose up -d postgres backend frontend
###
### Notes:
### - Run "Create vehicle token" before telemetry requests. It stores {{vehicleToken}} globally.
### - If token creation returns 409, that vehicle already has an unexpired active session.
###   Use another vehicle, wait for expiry, or mark the session inactive in Postgres for local testing.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@vehicleId = v-12
@otherVehicleId = v-13
@now = {{$isoTimestamp}}

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Fleet state
GET {{baseUrl}}/fleet/state

### All vehicles
GET {{baseUrl}}/vehicles

### Zone counts
GET {{baseUrl}}/zones/counts

### Recent anomalies
GET {{baseUrl}}/anomalies?limit=25

### Recent warnings
GET {{baseUrl}}/warnings?limit=25

### Anomalies for one vehicle
GET {{baseUrl}}/anomalies?vehicle_id={{vehicleId}}&limit=25

### Warnings for one vehicle
GET {{baseUrl}}/warnings?vehicle_id={{vehicleId}}&limit=25

### Create vehicle token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/vehicle-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vehicle_id": "{{vehicleId}}"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("vehicleToken", response.body.token);
  client.global.set("vehicleTokenExpiresAt", response.body.expires_at);
%}

### Valid telemetry with zone entry
POST {{baseUrl}}/telemetry
Authorization: Bearer {{vehicleToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vehicle_id": "{{vehicleId}}",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-24T00:00:00Z",
  "lat": 37.4100,
  "lon": -122.0800,
  "battery_pct": 78,
  "speed_mps": 1.2,
  "status": "moving",
  "error_codes": [],
  "zone_entered": "pack_station"
}

### Low battery warning, not anomaly
POST {{baseUrl}}/telemetry
Authorization: Bearer {{vehicleToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
